.SH NAME
cwal-templates \- template and backend format for cwal
.SH DESCRIPTION
Templates are plain text files rendered with the palette generated by
.BR cwal (1).
They are searched for, in order, in:
.PP
1. ${XDG_DATA_DIRS:-/usr/local/share:/usr/share}/cwal/templates (system-wide)
.br
2. ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/cwal/templates (user data)
.br
3. ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cwal/templates (user config)
.SH FORMAT SPECIFIERS
Color values are referenced with the format
.BI {color\fIN\fR .\fIFORMAT\fR}
where
.I N
is the color index (0-15) and
.I FORMAT
is one of:
.PP
.TS
l l l.
FORMAT	Description	Example (R=255,G=128,B=0,A=0.8)
_
hex	Hexadecimal #RRGGBB	#ff8000
xhex	Hexadecimal 0x prefix	0xff8000
strip	Hexadecimal without prefix	ff8000
rgb	RGB triplet	rgb(255,128,0)
rgba	RGBA with alpha	rgba(255,128,0,0.8)
hexa	Hexadecimal #RRGGBBAA	#ff8000cc
red	Red component (0-255)	255
green	Green component (0-255)	128
blue	Blue component (0-255)	0
.TE
.SH PLACEHOLDERS
Global placeholders can be used anywhere in a template:
.PP
.TS
l l l.
Placeholder	Description	Example
_
{mode}	Theme mode	dark
{wallpaper}	Absolute image path	/home/user/pic.jpg
{alpha}	Alpha value	0.80
{alpha.hex}	Alpha, 2-digit hex	cc
{alpha.pct}	Alpha, percentage	80
{alpha.int}	Alpha, 0-255 integer	204
{alpha.dec}	Alpha, decimal float	0.80
.TE
.PP
Example:
.nf
background = {color0.hex}
background_rgb = {color0.rgb}
foreground = {color1.strip}
.fi
.SH SURGICAL INJECTION
Instead of overwriting an entire configuration file, you can write the markers
.B $CWAL_START
and
.B $CWAL_END
into an existing file
(wrapped in the comment syntax of that file, e.g. \fB#\fR or \fB//\fR);
cwal replaces the text between them with the generated color block.
.SH BACKENDS
.B cwal
ships two built-in backends:
.PP
\fBcwal\fP \-\- The built-in default backend.
.PP
\fBlibimagequant\fP \-\- A libimagequant-based backend.
.PP
Additional backends can be written in Lua. Place a script defining a
.BR Main (image_path)
function that returns a table of 16 colors, each as an
.B {r, g, b}
table with integer components 0-255, in
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/cwal/backends/*.lua
(directory is created if missing).
The backend is then selected by its script filename without the
.B .lua
extension.
.PP
If the requested backend fails to process an image, cwal automatically falls
back to the other available backends in order.
See
.BR cwal (1)
and
.BR cwal " " \-\-list\-backends
for the list at runtime.
